 false}, {"t_ms": 10371, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01LdSa9eA2brNiff6iPaauJd", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 11858, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy. I did not use v2.3.1-rc, which was only in staging.\n- **Approval:** None was needed, since v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the rollback and lists next steps: confirm recovery and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01T1YJsmTpszQeXXDv6ToaLN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01941Xnbwn4oizEPQtLDu548", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0. v2.3.1 is the unhealthy release now running in all three regions. I'll roll back to v2.3.0, which has already been healthy in production, so it needs no change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01DeNh5Nyq8AzftNHoXWDgcd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015Rz6NFv5wenQEqzqaECqJr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LdSa9eA2brNiff6iPaauJd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18 before rollback). I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy and was not redeployed. Next steps: confirm error rate recovery on v2.3.0, and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy. No change-manager approval was needed because v2.3.0 was previously healthy in production.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is now healthy with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18 on v2.3.1.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 is marked unhealthy. I did not use v2.3.1-rc, which was only in staging.\n- **Approval:** None was needed, since v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged the on-call engineer. It describes the rollback and lists next steps: confirm recovery and investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy.", "type": "text"}]}]}